17428171,2025-11-21,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"MOHELAs additional research needed response is unacceptable and is a direct violation of federal law. This is a stall tactic and does not meet the requirements of the Fair Credit Reporting Act.

Under 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), a furnisher and CRA have 30 days to complete a reasonable investigation. They can not extend this period simply because they do not have the records, and they can not continue reporting information that is unverified, disputed, or incomplete.

Equifax already deleted this same MOHELA account after CFPB intervention. That proves the information is unverifiable. If it cant be verified for one bureau, it can not be verified for any bureau. Continuing to report unverified data violates 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) ( failure to maintain maximum accuracy ) and 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( b ) ( failure of the furnisher to investigate and correct inaccurate information ).

MOHELAs inability to produce documentation within the required window is not my problem.

The law is clear : If verification can not be produced, the account MUST be deleted.

Anything else is a violation.

I am requesting CFPB enforcement for the following : Immediate deletion of the MOHELA account from TransUnion due to failure to verify within the statutory timeframe.

A determination that MOHELA is in violation of 1681i, 1681e ( b ), and 1681s-2 ( b ).

Written proof of what MOHELA claims to be researching, since they have already exceeded the lawful period for investigation.

Confirmation that TransUnion stops reporting disputed and unverified information, per FCRA 1681c-2.

MOHELA has had more than enough time. Their inability to provide evidence is not additional researchit is noncompliance. The FCRA does not allow companies to drag out investigations indefinitely to avoid deleting inaccurate information.

I am demanding immediate action.",Company believes it acted appropriately as authorized by contract or law,MOHELA,IL,610XX,,Web,2025-11-21,Closed with explanation,Yes
